Portions are adapted from SGLang (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang): the stock
decode step of DeepSeek-V4.1 (the layer loop, the mHC boundaries, the attention, the
MoE, Engram and the head) follows SGLang's own model code (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright SGLang Team). Each adapted file names its origin in its header.

Portions are adapted from FlashInfer (https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer):
the Lamport all-reduce primitives and the low-latency all-reduce (Apache License
2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 by FlashInfer team), and the epilogue of the wo_b GEMM
that publishes into the all-reduce mailbox (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2026
NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES; the full notice is kept in that file). Each
adapted file names its origin in its header. The Kimi K3 split-K GEMM in
sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k3/cutedsl/gemm/splitk.py is adapted from FlashInfer's
flashinfer/gemm/kernels/dense_bf16_gemm_sm100_splitk.py at v0.7.0.post1
(Apache License 2.0). FlashInfer's NOTICE file reads:

FlashInfer
Copyright 2025-2026 NVIDIA
Copyright 2023-2026 FlashInfer community (https://flashinfer.ai/)

Portions of the Kimi K3 kernels are adapted from vLLM
(https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors
to the vLLM project), commit 642c18d64c4cb6db3ded8fbe1786718cd4005fcb:
sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k3/cutedsl/gemm/splitk_tmem8.py and splitk_tmem64.py
build on vLLM's SplitKGemm (which vLLM adapted from FlashInfer
v0.7.0.post1 dense_bf16_gemm_sm100_splitk.py); moe/wide_plan.py reuses methods
of vLLM's ExpertsPlanKernel; and
the vendored rubin/ package holds vLLM files, unmodified or modified, and NVIDIA
files with portions adapted from vLLM. Each file names its origin in its header;
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt lists them.

Portions of the Kimi K3.1 code are adapted from other projects. Each file names its
origin in its header, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt lists the files and the terms:

- sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k31/dsa/dg_logits.cuh is DeepGEMM's
  deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm100_mqa_logits.cuh from sgl-deep-gemm
  0.2.3.post2 with additions marked "K3.1:" (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025
  DeepSeek). The MIT License text is in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.
- sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k31/dsa/dg_include/deep_gemm/ holds unmodified copies of the
  sgl-deep-gemm 0.2.3.post2 headers that dg_logits.cuh includes (MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2025 DeepSeek); dg_include/README.md names their origin.
- sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k31/dsa/x47960/ holds a modified copy of SGLang's DeepSeek-V4
  top-k kernels from public SGLang commit b2833196d8 (Apache License 2.0, Copyright
  SGLang Team); its __init__.py lists the six local edits, each marked "k31 edit" in
  the files. topk_v2_tkpush.cuh there is a second copy of topk_v2.cuh with further
  NVIDIA additions marked "k31 TKPUSH", also listed in __init__.py. That code credits
  vLLM's csrc/persistent_topk.cuh (Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors to the
  vLLM project) and FlashInfer's include/flashinfer/topk.cuh (Apache License 2.0).
- The exact top-k merge in sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k31/dsa/tsi.cuh, and select_kth and
  the (score, position) key in tsim.cuh and tsim_lean.cuh next to it, are adapted from
  SGLang's python/sglang/kernels/jit/csrc/dsa/dcp_topk_merge.cuh at commit
  f3532057e15f (Apache License 2.0).
- sgl_nvidia_mega/kimi_k31/dsa/gvr2/ holds FlashInfer's gvr_2 top-k
  (flashinfer/topk_varlen/kernels/gvr2_topk_{host,decode}.py, Apache License 2.0),
  which FlashInfer ported from TensorRT-LLM pull request 17821 (Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION). The host file is unmodified; the decode
  file carries an NVIDIA modification marked in the file. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
  names the exact FlashInfer revision.
